WEBVTT

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.210
The government in this 
world is so serious.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.270
What's wrong, Matsukaze?

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.340
Okay, got it.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:31.630
Let's hurry.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:59.790
That's the Saturday Night Rider?

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:57.690
Sanctuary

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.690
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.450
<i>I have to go to the bathroom!</i>

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.770
I can go, right?

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.200
It'll be okay, right?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.210
<i>I can do it! I can do it! 
It'll be fine!</i>

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.900
Don't ignore us, old lady.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.390
We hate being treated like we're 
not here more than anything.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:33.800
You understand?

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.990
I apologize. I'm sorry. So sorry!

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:41.650
Well, if you're not going 
to ignore us, you can pass.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.010
Thanks so much...

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.990
Hey, she's a teacher at Gami!

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:51.130
What?

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.810
If you do anything to me,

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:57.090
I'll tell the education committee, 
not just the school!

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.430
The education committee?

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:02.840
What are you gonna tell 'em?

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.500
Well, just if you do something...

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:09.100
And I bet you're going to tell them 
all sorts of lies while you're at it.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:13.060
No, I won't, I think...

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:17.090
Then it would be a mistake 
to just let you go.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.120
Yeah! Definitely!

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.060
Tragic.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.800
Truly tragic.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:35.090
Who are you?

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.710
Bike riders are the kabukimono 
of this age, right?

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.470
And yet you're attacking 
people at random.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.080
The only word I can think of is tragic.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:50.950
So, is this a game?

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.090
Or are you serious?

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:57.230
If you're serious, you're ready to 
wear the white clothing, right?

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.790
White clothing?

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:02.130
If you're prepared to pick 
a fight with Maeda Keiji,

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:06.130
then you're ready to lay 
down your life, right?

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.140
The Saturday Night Rider was so cool!

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:37.390
So you saw the Saturday 
Night Rider, Futagawa-san.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.720
The mysterious bike rider,

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.940
who appears every Saturday 
and beats up delinquents.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.650
Lately, everybody's talking about her.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:50.330
A beautiful woman in a gorgeous 
kimono, on a huge, black bike!

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.250
She was just like everybody said.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:56.430
Yamaguchi-san.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:59.250
Stop talking about nonsense and get to work.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.280
Right.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:09.850
The Saturday Night Rider?

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.810
So stupid.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:14.260
Good evening, Yamaguchi-san.

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:15.980
Aren't you always supposed

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.970
to greet me with 
"good morning," Maeda-san?

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:21.640
Well, I was a little late,

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:24.100
so I didn't think "good 
morning" was right.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.840
Then don't be late.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.110
Sorry.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:34.370
Are you interested in the 
Saturday Night Rider, too?

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.450
The Saturday Night... what?

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:41.660
Does it have something to do with work?

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:44.040
I guess not.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.730
Get to your place.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:46.880
R-Right.

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:52.190
Oota-san, Oota-san.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.640
Potato Chips is here.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.230
You're right.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:59.140
He's here every day.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.880
He must really love potato chips.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:02.990
He's coming!

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.150
Welcome.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:08.150
Thank you.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.290
He bought three again today.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.470
Yeah.

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.410
Hello!

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:19.080
We're here to bring in the shipment!

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.410
Shipment!

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.800
Thank you so much.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.920
We'll leave it here.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:28.660
Goodbye!

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.920
I guess those girls are 
fine, for beginners.

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:42.360
Maeda-san.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:45.150
Phone off during working hours.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.920
But it might be something important.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:50.780
Maeda-san?

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:53.380
Hello?

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:56.330
Hello? Is this the 
Saturday Night Rider?

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.790
Oh, you.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:01.020
Hey, don't be so cold.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:04.280
Sorry. I'm working now.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.300
Then I'll be quick.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.610
I want to thank you for yesterday.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:09.800
Will you meet me?

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:13.530
I'm working now, so I'm hanging up.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:14.990
Hey!

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.770
I shouldn't have given her my number.

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:21.730
She said she was a teacher,

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:24.750
so I thought she'd have better manners.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:27.150
Hey, did you hear?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:30.900
Mori-san from Sanctuary's 
gonna take 3 months to heal.

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:35.120
So what's Mizuki-san gonna do about it?

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.990
Not a thing, he says!

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.910
Is Sanctuary really gonna 
be okay like that?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.620
<i>If they're talking about 
"Sanctuary," does that mean</i>

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.920
<i>they're with the guys from last night?</i>

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.190
What is it, old lady?

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:51.420
You want something?

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:54.050
I don't mind you talking,

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:57.530
but do you think you could 
do it a little farther away?

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:00.330
We're customers, too.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.650
Do you have a problem?

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.100
Please.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:15.200
Neither of us would want this 
place going out of business.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:19.050
Y-Yeah.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:21.950
We wouldn't want it going out 
of business because of us.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.880
Hey, guys, let's head a bit farther away.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.800
Are you okay, Maeda-san?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.300
Yes, I'm fine.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:39.000
Aren't you scared of those thugs?

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.120
I can't believe you went 
up and talked to them!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.800
Well, they can't be in front 
of the store like that.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:44.770
They can't?

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:48.060
They don't suit our store's image.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.770
They don't?

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:52.540
I'm gonna go change.

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:55.920
Okay, leave the register to me!

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.640
I'm bad with math, though!

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:01.490
Is this stuff gonna come out?

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:03.780
Kids these days.

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:05.290
They do the craziest stuff.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:11.020
If they did it to a customer, 
I would've made them regret it.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.300
Shut up!

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:16.420
Give me the money!

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:18.990
Now a robber?

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:20.930
This place sure is busy.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.680
Well, I guess I'll go save them.

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:38.480
Give me the money!

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:40.640
Um, well...

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.520
I don't really remember what 
the manual says for robbers,

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:45.860
so can I go read it?

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:47.200
Of course not!

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:49.210
Give me the money!

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:51.910
<i>The enemy's got a ranged weapon.</i>

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.040
<i>Well, it'll work out.</i>

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.610
What do we do?

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:57.990
What do you mean?

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.410
What the?!

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:02.730
It's dark!

00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:16.670
Did you defeat the robber?

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:18.060
That's amazing.

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:19.610
I did?

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:24.370
I think one of my punches 
hit in the darkness...

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.640
There was another robber 
not too long ago.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:29.430
What is it with this place?

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:33.010
I guess a lot of strange people 
come to this convenience store.

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.840
Well, I suppose that applies to you, too.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.200
Do you think so?

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:43.590
I wish the Saturday Night Rider 
had come instead of a robber...

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:49.180
Yeah, but they're so violent that
they'd just cause a big ruckus instead.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:52.840
But don't you think a 
ruckus might be fun?

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:56.610
I'm kind of plain, so I've always 
wanted to do something like that.

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:58.420
I know!

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:00.050
They say peace is best.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:02.460
But too much peace is boring.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:04.690
So you agree, Futagawa-san...

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.830
What do you think, Yamaguchi-san?

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.820
As long as it doesn't involve me.

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:11.410
But you are interested, aren't you?

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:15.960
Get back to work.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:26.510
Welcome.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:30.270
<i>It's one of the guys who was 
out front the other day.</i>

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:37.270
<i>Looks like he's just here to shop.</i>

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:44.410
Are you going to wear these yourself?

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:47.530
It's none of your business, old lady.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:52.080
Ring me up already.

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:54.520
Ring me up, I said!

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.590
Are you deaf, old lady?

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:59.960
That's right.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.810
Matsuura-san, I've got a request.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:16.470
Anything you want, Keiji!

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:17.570
Do you want me to

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:20.200
dress up all sexy and 
distract some riders?

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.790
Not at all.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.110
I want you to find the address 
of one of these thugs.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:28.370
One of my students?

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:32.030
Yeah. I'll send you something 
describing him later.

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:33.260
Can you do it?

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:34.850
Well, yeah.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.560
But you've gotta go on 
a date with me later.

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:39.750
Fine.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.290
Okay, get it for me by Saturday night.

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:42.990
Okay!

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:48.190
<i>He's my target this weekend.</i>

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:50.830
Maeda-san.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.220
No phone calls during work.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:56.640
Sorry.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.900
Date: 2012/06/23
From: Matsuura
Sub: Here's the address! ♥

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:01.900
Kudou from 2-B, huh?

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:06.900
This address is near where 
I went three weeks ago.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.910
To:

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.910
<b>The Date

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.910
When?

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.910
Keiji

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:09.910
<b>Sending</b>

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:13.090
<i>Even kabukimono have rules.</i>

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:16.660
<i>That goes for kabukimono 
in this era, too.</i>

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:37.850
Let's go, Matsukaze!

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.570
No.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.030
Not her, either.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.310
What am I doing?

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:59.040
Even if the Saturday Night 
Rider actually came, so what?

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:10.970
But you are interested, aren't you?

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:18.890
Hey, that hurt, miss.

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.780
What?

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:22.650
You ran into me!

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:26.650
That hurts when you say that, really.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:29.510
Come with me.

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:30.390
What are you doing?!

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:31.780
Stop!

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:33.870
Let me go! Let me go!

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:35.920
Stop!

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:36.750
Somebody!

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:38.120
Somebody help me!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.870
Somebody! Somebody!

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:44.630
Somebody save me...

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:51.630
What are you doing?

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:55.080
When I said I wanted to go someplace private,

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:56.930
you nodded, right?

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.770
I did not!

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:03.670
They really do need to be lively 
like you, or it's no fun.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:14.160
We can play tag for a little 
while longer, miss!

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.080
<i>Why?</i>

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:17.160
<i>Why?</i>

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:22.620
<i>Why is this happening to me?</i>

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.440
Why me?

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.970
Nobody's here.

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:40.000
And even if they were, 
they wouldn't help you.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:45.100
You understand, right, miss?

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:51.110
That's right.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:57.570
Nobody helped me on the way here.

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:01.630
Nobody cares about 
anybody but themselves.

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:04.630
You can run, but don't struggle.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:08.170
You don't want to get hurt, do you?

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:11.510
<i>What's he saying?</i>

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:14.590
<i>But I can't do anything.</i>

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.520
<i>Nobody will save me!</i>

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:20.840
<i>They won't save me!</i>

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.980
Got you!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:25.810
Now stay still.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.480
No! Stop!

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:48.290
I wondered why Matsukaze 
told me to go this way.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:50.290
So this was why.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:54.170
I lost control for a second and hit him,

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:56.550
but I don't think he's dead.

00:17:56.830 --> 00:18:01.250
But he won't be able to move for 
a while, so don't worry, miss.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:02.930
Thank you.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:05.830
Thank Matsukaze.

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:08.560
He's the one who told me to save you.

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:12.240
Matsukaze? Is there somebody else here?

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.680
No, he's my bike.

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:17.680
He told me you were in trouble.

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:18.530
Your bike did?

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:21.460
You can talk with your bike?

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:23.580
Well, just kinda.

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:27.340
I'm sure if you rode, 
you would understand.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:39.090
I think I hate myself.

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:43.210
I've been so serious, 
even though I don't really mean to.

00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:45.460
And my employees hate me...

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:51.220
I was so serious today, 
and nobody came to save me!

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:54.610
Then it's simple.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:57.220
Live how you want to.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.110
That's right.

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:04.870
It's strange.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:08.120
I've never been this open 
to a person I've just met.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.150
It's like I'm not myself.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.470
Everyone's more open when 
Matsukaze's around.

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:18.630
What's your name?

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:20.830
The Saturday Night Rider.

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:23.140
That's enough, right?

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:26.640
By the way, can I have 
a little of your time?

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:29.030
I want to finish something.

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.140
Huh?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.350
<b>Kudou</b>

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:36.560
Hey.

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:39.240
Wha—

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:40.660
Who are you?!

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:43.910
Hey, you awake, Kudou-kun?

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.040
What is this?

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:48.380
Who are you?

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:50.360
The Saturday Night Rider.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:53.020
The one who destroyed the Sanctuary?

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:55.540
That makes this fast.

00:19:55.990 --> 00:19:58.700
But what did I do to you?

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:02.900
Tragic. So tragic.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:06.060
A young man who doesn't even 
understand what he's done wrong.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:09.430
So what did I do?

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:13.190
If you don't know, then I'll tell you!

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:20.780
Look at this pure white underwear!

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:25.950
Are you a pervert?

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:31.280
Even after seeing this pure white 
underwear, you don't understand?

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:33.240
Of course not!

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:35.630
A kabukimono must wear white underwear!

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:43.510
Underwear is the last piece of 
clothing you wear in your life.

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:46.510
It's just like the clothes 
you wear when you're dead.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.820
Maybe, but is that enough 
reason to come to my house?

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:51.140
And in the middle of the night?!

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:53.450
It's my job as your elder

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:57.470
to teach you modern kabukimono the rules.

00:20:57.470 --> 00:20:58.150
Right?

00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:03.000
Kudou-kun.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:04.550
If you're not going to change your ways,

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:06.500
I'll be back next week.

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:07.480
Got it?

00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:08.760
Okay.

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:10.400
Good.

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:17.800
So that's why the guys you 
go after never say anything.

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:22.470
Well, most men would be too 
embarrassed to say anything.

00:21:22.470 --> 00:21:23.740
Yeah.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:27.900
Um... will we see each other again?

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:31.680
Matsukaze will bring me to 
you when the time comes.

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:49.240
Okay.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.060
What happened?

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:55.270
I don't have a clue. Yeah.

00:21:56.030 --> 00:21:58.670
By the way, what color 
is your underwear?

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:01.580
My underwear?

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:04.760
I've always worn white.

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:06.040
I see.

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:08.970
I think you and I can be friends.

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:10.550
Yes.

00:23:47.270 --> 00:23:50.280
So next time, it's the Silver 
Hornet, Sugitani Zenjibou?

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:54.780
Next time on Sengoku 
Collection: "Silver Hornet."

00:23:54.780 --> 00:23:57.240
Listen. When you're ready to watch it,

00:23:57.240 --> 00:23:59.280
wear white underwear!
